-### Button group classes
-
-The button group key ships whole, in its own partial: the horizontal group, the vertical group, the
-relationships that join their children, and the sized group families. It declares no custom property
-of its own. Its radius reads `--bs-border-radius` and its overlap reads `--bs-border-width`, and
-the `_tokens.scss` partial already declares each of those over `--vn-radius-base` and
-`--vn-border-width`, so a consumer retuning either name moves the group.
-
-A group lays its children out as an inline flex line, and each child grows and shrinks from an
-automatic basis, so the children share the group's free space. The vertical group turns that line
-into a column, aligns it to the leading edge, and stretches every child to the group's own width.
-
-Neighbouring children overlap rather than doubling their shared border: each child after the first
-is pulled back by one border width, on the inline axis in a horizontal group and on the block axis
-in a vertical one. A child the reader is addressing lifts over that shared border, and the states
-that lift it are a checked or focused `.btn-check` input's label, a hovered child, a focused child,
-a pressed child, and a child carrying `.active`.
-
-The corners follow the same physical reading. A horizontal group clears the trailing corners of
-every child but the last and the leading corners of every child but the first, so the group keeps
-one rounded outline; a vertical group clears the bottom corners and the top corners the same way. A
-group nested inside a group is treated as one of those children, and its own children carry the
-corners it would have carried. A child carrying the `.dropdown-toggle` class keeps its trailing
-corners, which is what leaves room for the split toggle Disclosure ships.
-
-The `.btn-group-sm > .btn` and `.btn-group-lg > .btn` twins ship from the
-`src/styles/components/_button.scss` partial, where Bootstrap's own `@extend` rule puts them, so the
-sized group families resolve the Button size each name declares and this partial writes nothing for
-them.
-
-The `tests/src/styles/components/button-group.test.ts` proof reads each resolved treatment in the
-browser: the direction and child growth, the overlap measured as the offset between neighbours,
-every corner of every child position, the excluded `.dropdown-toggle` child read against a plain
-child in each direction, each lift driven or written, the label of a focused input that is still
-unchecked, the retuned compatibility variables, and the published radius and density factors. The
-lift a pressed child takes is read out of the cascade as well as rendered: the pointer driver moves
-onto its target before pressing it, so the rendered reading alone cannot tell the pressed selector
-from the hovered one that lifts the same child.
-
-These are the key's recorded departures.
-
-- **The split-toggle selectors are absent.** Each of them belongs to the split toggle Disclosure
-  owns, and § Deferred selectors carries a row for each. That table is where they are enumerated, so
-  a name withheld under this key is read there rather than written twice.
-- **The shown-group shadow is absent from the release as well.** Bootstrap writes
-  `.btn-group.show .dropdown-toggle` through its shadow mixin, and that mixin emits nothing while
-  shadows are off, so the official cascade carries no such rule and neither does this one.
