-### Spinner classes
-
-The spinner key ships whole: the border spinner, the grow spinner, and their small twins. One rule
-declares the box each spinner shares, and each name declares the speed and the animation it runs, so
-a consumer retunes either spinner through `--bs-spinner-animation-speed` and reaches the shared box
-through `--bs-spinner-width` and `--bs-spinner-height`.
-
-The border spinner paints a ring from `currentcolor` with a transparent right edge, and the grow
-spinner paints a filled circle that scales from nothing, so each one takes its color from the text
-around it.
-
-Under the reduced-motion preference each spinner slows to `1.5s` and keeps turning. A spinner
-reports that work is still running, so a still ring would report the opposite of what the component
-exists to say, and this is Bootstrap's own recorded behavior. The preference retunes the same speed
-property a consumer retunes, which is why the animation itself is declared once.
-
-The rotation is physical: the ring turns the same way whatever the document's writing direction, so
-the direction-flipping annotation the release carries on that keyframe does not ship.
-
-The `tests/src/styles/components/spinner.test.ts` proof reads the resolved box, border, paint, and
-running animation in the browser, under each motion preference and in each color mode.
