+### Breadcrumb classes
+
+The breadcrumb key ships whole: the trail, the inset between items, the divider each item after the
+first paints before itself, and the current page the `active` class marks.
+
+The trail is a wrapping flex row carrying no list marker, so an `ol` element renders as a line of
+steps that wraps at its container's edge. Its bottom margin reads `--vn-space-8` and the inset
+between items reads `--vn-space-4`, so both rescale with `--vn-factor-density`. The trail's own
+padding is zero on each axis, and every remaining length is Bootstrap's own literal.
+
+The divider is the leading content of each item after the first, written as
+`var(--bs-breadcrumb-divider, "/")`. The cascade declares that property nowhere, so the slash is the
+fallback the rule carries, and a consumer replaces the divider by declaring the property on the
+trail. The pseudo-element floats to the physical start, so the divider sits ahead of its item's text
+whatever the document's writing direction.
+
+The fill and the radius are declared with nothing after the colon, which is what Bootstrap writes:
+each property stands so a consumer can set it, and each declaration reading it resolves as unset
+until one does. `--bs-breadcrumb-font-size` is declared nowhere, for the same reason Bootstrap
+declares it nowhere, so the `font-size` declaration reading it leaves the trail at its inherited
+size.
+
+The divider color and the `active` item's color both read `--bs-secondary-color`, which each color
+mode declares for itself, so a trail inside a dark island follows the island.
+
+The `tests/src/styles/components/breadcrumb.test.ts` proof reads each resolved treatment in the
+browser.
