+### Badge classes
+
+The badge key ships whole: the label box, the empty collapse, and the offset a badge takes inside a
+button.
+
+The font size and the padding are relative, and so is the `em` box they make. The font size is
+`0.75em` of the host, and the padding is `0.65em` and `0.35em` of the badge's own size, so the two
+multiply and the box sizes itself from whatever text it sits in. The line height is the unitless
+`1`, so the label's line box is the badge's own font size rather than the body rhythm. The offset a
+badge takes inside a button is the absolute `-1px` Bootstrap writes, so it moves with no text size.
+The radius reads `--bs-border-radius`, which this cascade declares over `--vn-radius-base`, so
+`--vn-factor-radius` reaches a badge whose own rule names no Veneer token.
+
+The label color reads `--vn-palette-white-base`, which holds Bootstrap's own `#fff`. The class
+declares no fill at all, which is Bootstrap's own treatment: a badge paints its label over whatever
+surface carries it, and a contextual fill class supplies the rest. Veneer ships no such class, so
+the showcase paints each badge specimen on a dark table surface.
+
+An empty badge collapses, and a badge inside a button lifts by one pixel. Both are Bootstrap's own
+rules, and the offset selects `.btn .badge` rather than the badge class, so a badge outside a button
+stays in flow.
+
+The `tests/src/styles/components/badge.test.ts` proof reads each resolved treatment in the browser.
